<section class="content-section" id="overview-section">
    <div class="content-container">
        <div class="text-content">
            <h2 class="section-title">LLP Agreement Change for Delhi LLPs</h2>
            <div class="content-text">
                <div class="highlight-box" style="margin-bottom:20px;">
                    <p><strong>&#128204; TL;DR - LLP Agreement Change in Delhi Services at a Glance</strong></p>
                    <p>LLP Agreement is internal constitution. Changes require: (1) all partners agree, (2) Supplementary Deed on Delhi stamp paper (Rs 100-500), signed by all, notarised, (3) Form 3 on MCA V3 within 30 days. Common changes: profit sharing, partner addition/removal (Form 4), capital, business activity, office (Form 15), name (Form 5). Late: Rs 100/day no cap. No limit on amendments. Patron manages from Delhi.</p>
                </div>
                <p>Delhi LLPs frequently amend agreements: professional firms restructuring profit shares, startups adding partners, firms diversifying activities, offices relocating. Without proper agreement, First Schedule defaults apply (equal sharing). Learn more about <a href="/llp-agreement-change">LLP Agreement Change across India</a>.</p>
                <p>Patron Accounting's Delhi office handles complete amendment: supplementary deed, stamp duty, notarisation, Form 3, linked forms. Integrated with <a href="/llp-incorporation">LLP registration</a>, <a href="/pvt-llp-compliance">LLP compliance</a>, and <a href="/legal-drafting">legal drafting</a>.</p>
                <p>Content is reviewed quarterly for accuracy.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<!-- SECTION 3: WHAT IS GSTAT APPEAL FILING -->
<section class="content-section" id="what-section">
    <div class="content-container">
        <div class="two-column">
            <div class="column-content">
                <h2 class="section-title">Section 23 of the LLP Act, 2008</h2>
                <div class="content-text what-is-definition">
                    
                    <p>LLP Agreement (S.2(1)(o)) is any written agreement between partners determining mutual rights, duties, and obligations. Under S.23(1), mutual rights governed by agreement. Under S.23(2), agreement and changes filed with ROC via Form 3 within 30 days.</p><p>Not available for public inspection (unlike company MOA/AOA). Can be amended unlimited times. Each amendment requires Supplementary LLP Agreement on stamp paper, signed by all partners, notarised.</p><p>Patron drafts and files all amendments for Delhi LLPs — no generic templates.</p>

                </div>
                <div class="highlight-box" style="margin-top:20px;">
                    <p><strong>Key Terms for LLP Agreement Change in Delhi:</strong></p>
                    <p><strong>Form 3:</strong> Filed within 30 days. MCA V3. Designated partner DSC. Supplementary deed attached.</p><p><strong>Supplementary Deed:</strong> Delhi stamp paper (Rs 100-500). All partners sign. Notarised.</p><p><strong>Linked Forms:</strong> Form 4 (partners). Form 5 (name). Form 15 (address). Filed simultaneously.</p><p><strong>Penalty:</strong> Rs 100/day no cap. 1 year late = Rs 36,500. Informal changes unenforceable.</p>

                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="column-image">
                <div class="illustration-placeholder">
                    <div class="illustration-icon" style="max-width:240px;">
                        <svg viewBox="0 0 200 180" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
                            <!-- Building / Tribunal -->
